From 7558a8cabb11de86120982da05c1d3a75ac462b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yiliu Dong <91178480+qianlihuang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:46:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] [MoE] SM90 MegaMoE: default workspace without DP counts;
 test fixes

- Every EP rank must launch on the same workspace. Without the DP-wide
  token counts in the forward context, the adapter now uses the default
  workspace instead of sizing it from the local batch.
- The rebuild test passes the kernel weights by name and checks that the
  rebuilt layer reads the same storage.
- The GPU test runs the modular kernel under inference mode and a forward
  context with DP-wide token counts, as serving does. It now covers the
  GLM-5.3-Flash, DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, Kimi-K3 and Qwen3.8-Flash-Next
  expert shapes.
- The weight-layout and router-weight tests move next to the other kernel
  tests. Stale comments are fixed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Yiliu Dong <91178480+qianlihuang@users.noreply.github.com>
